From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:10:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add shadow-root node model (NodeData::ShadowRoot + host
 linkage)

Groundwork for native shadow DOM: a shadow root is a slab node that
lives outside its host's child list (the template_contents pattern),
carrying host back-pointer + open/closed mode. ElementData gains the
shadow_root slot pointing at it. No behavior change yet - nothing
creates these nodes; attach_shadow, flat-tree traversal, and scoped
styling land in follow-up patches. Match arms added where NodeData
is matched exhaustively (inline-box scan tolerates a stray shadow
root rather than panicking the paint; the embedder recovers from
unwinds, but a poisoned paint helps nobody).

Upstreaming note: DioxusLabs/blitz roadmap #119 lists shadow DOM as
wanted-but-unstarted; if upstreamed this would grow an opt-in feature
gate like the bot-proposed PR #478 had.
